- **Reasoning**: The standard categorizes all life cycle processes into these four distinct groups to organize how systems are acquired, supplied, enabled, managed, and technically realized. 
- **Citation**: 
"This document groups the activities that can be performed during the life cycle of a system into four process groups:
- a) agreement processes;
- b) organizational project-enabling processes;
- c) technical management processes;
- d) technical processes."
(ISO/IEC/IEEE 15288, Section 5.7.1, pp. 28–29)

